@host = http://localhost:5000

### 1. GET All Quizlets (Should be empty initially, then have data after POST)
GET {{host}}/api/quizlets
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. POST Create Quizlet (Upload Excel)
# Note: You need to use the actual path to your valid_quiz_data.xlsx file
# or use Postman for easier file uploading.
# This HTTP file syntax for file upload works with VS Code "REST Client" extension if configured correctly,
# but usually Postman is recommended for Multipart forms.

# curl equivalent:
# curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/quizlets \
#   -F "title=Test Quiz from Curl" \
#   -F "description=Created via command line" \
#   -F "isPublished=true" \
#   -F "listQuestion=@valid_quiz_data.xlsx"

### 4. PUT Update Quizlet
# Replace 1 with the actual ID you want to update
PUT {{host}}/api/quizlets/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Title via API",
  "isPublished": true,
  "listQuestion": [
    {
      "content": "Updated Question 1",
      "score": 1,
      "answers": ["Option A", "Option B", "Option C", "Option D"],
      "correctAnswers": ["Option A"],
      "questionType": "MultipleChoice"
    },
    {
      "content": "New Question 2",
      "score": 2,
      "answers": ["True", "False"],
      "correctAnswers": ["True"],
      "questionType": "SingleChoice"
    }
  ]
}

### 5. GET Student Quizlets (Published Only)
GET {{host}}/api/students/quizlets
Content-Type: application/json
